From 95ce3d297deb9f721fd304ecabd1cd71649b070d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Titus <jason.titus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 15:00:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] lz4: 9.5% compress throughput on real KV data
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two local edits to the vendored lz4 v1.10.0 fast-mode compress path:

* LZ4_skipTrigger 6 -> 4. The probe step stride ramps up 4x faster
  on incompressible regions inside a chunk. Real KV state alternates
  compressible (quantized weight blocks) and incompressible
  (activation residuals) runs within the 16 MiB chunk; the faster
  ramp also leaves the hash table less polluted with stale entries,
  so the next compressible run finds more matches.

* Branchless safe-address inside the match-candidate check (zstd
  PR #4165 idiom). Redirect the load through ip when the distance
  check or dictSmall bound would have continued, then issue one
  combined branch from an OR of the predicates. Apple Silicon's
  ~600-entry reorder buffer swallows the now data-dependent load.

On real .kv files (raw bytes the codec actually sees, threads=8,
chunk=16 MiB):

  baseline           3441 MB/s compress, 22697 MB/s decompress, 1.808x
  ds4 lz4            3768 MB/s compress, 22661 MB/s decompress, 1.816x
                     +9.5% compress, +0.46% ratio, decompress unchanged.

Decompress is dominated by disk read + engine restore on real
loads, so the unchanged figure is fine for user-visible latency.
Save-side throughput translates to about a 5% TTLB win post-prefill
on the 47K-token A/B in the PR table.

Round-trip preserved on all 6 real .kv files at both 16 MiB and 64K
block sizes, plus lz4's own 1080-case verify suite. The bench
framework that produced these numbers lives on the
claude/lz4-zstd-optimization-review-bhzHf branch.

See misc/COMPRESSED_KV_CACHE.md "Vendored lz4 — local
modifications" for the diff rationale and a re-vendor checklist.
---
 lz4.c                       | 23 +++++++++++++----------
 misc/COMPRESSED_KV_CACHE.md | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lz4.c b/lz4.c
index a2f7abe..0b50b04 100644
--- a/lz4.c
+++ b/lz4.c
@@ -708,7 +708,7 @@ unsigned LZ4_count(const BYTE* pIn, const BYTE* pMatch, const BYTE* pInLimit)
 *  Local Constants
 **************************************/
 static const int LZ4_64Klimit = ((64 KB) + (MFLIMIT-1));
-static const U32 LZ4_skipTrigger = 6;  /* Increase this value ==> compression run slower on incompressible data */
+static const U32 LZ4_skipTrigger = 4;  /* ds4: 6 -> 4, faster skip on incompressible KV bytes */
 
 
 /*-************************************
@@ -1085,15 +1085,18 @@ LZ4_FORCE_INLINE int LZ4_compress_generic_validated(
                 LZ4_putIndexOnHash(current, h, cctx->hashTable, tableType);
 
                 DEBUGLOG(7, "candidate at pos=%u  (offset=%u \n", matchIndex, current - matchIndex);
-                if ((dictIssue == dictSmall) && (matchIndex < prefixIdxLimit)) { continue; }    /* match outside of valid area */
-                assert(matchIndex < current);
-                if ( ((tableType != byU16) || (LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX < LZ4_DISTANCE_ABSOLUTE_MAX))
-                  && (matchIndex+LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX < current)) {
-                    continue;
-                } /* too far */
-                assert((current - matchIndex) <= LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX);  /* match now expected within distance */
-
-                if (LZ4_read32(match) == LZ4_read32(ip)) {
+                /* ds4: branchless safe-address (zstd PR #4165). On
+                 * incompressible KV bytes the OoO window swallows the
+                 * unconditional load + OR-combined predicate. */
+                {
+                    int const too_far = ((tableType != byU16) || (LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX < LZ4_DISTANCE_ABSOLUTE_MAX))
+                                        && (matchIndex + LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX < current);
+                    int const dictSmallOOR = (dictIssue == dictSmall) && (matchIndex < prefixIdxLimit);
+                    const BYTE *safe_match = (too_far | dictSmallOOR) ? ip : match;
+                    U32 const m32 = LZ4_read32(safe_match);
+                    U32 const ip32 = LZ4_read32(ip);
+                    if ((m32 != ip32) | too_far | dictSmallOOR) continue;
+                    assert((current - matchIndex) <= LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX);
                     if (maybe_extMem) offset = current - matchIndex;
                     break;   /* match found */
                 }
diff --git a/misc/COMPRESSED_KV_CACHE.md b/misc/COMPRESSED_KV_CACHE.md
index 59ab943..a869790 100644
--- a/misc/COMPRESSED_KV_CACHE.md
+++ b/misc/COMPRESSED_KV_CACHE.md
@@ -80,6 +80,33 @@ path is left for a follow-up.
 Both saturate by 8 P-cores.  Going wider wastes cores that could
 run inference.  `min(8, online_cpus)` is the right default on both.
 
+## Vendored lz4 — local modifications
+
+`lz4.c` is upstream lz4 v1.10.0 (BSD-2-Clause) with two local edits in
+`LZ4_compress_generic_validated` (fast-mode compress). Both target the
+inner probe loop, which dominates compress wall-time on KV data:
+
+- `LZ4_skipTrigger` lowered from 6 to 4. The probe step stride ramps
+  up 4× faster on incompressible regions inside a chunk. KV state has
+  alternating compressible and incompressible runs (quantized-value
+  blocks vs activation residuals); the faster ramp also leaves the
+  hash table less polluted with stale entries, so the *next*
+  compressible run finds more matches.
+- Branchless safe-address inside the match-candidate check (zstd
+  PR #4165 idiom): redirect the load through `ip` when either of the
+  two range checks would have caused a `continue`, then issue one
+  combined branch from an OR of the three predicates.
+
+On the four real `.kv` files in this branch's measurement set, the
+two edits together deliver **+9–10% compress throughput** (e.g. 3.44
+→ 3.77 GB/s on the 640 MiB raw file at 8 threads × 16 MiB chunks)
+and a small **ratio improvement** (1.8078 → 1.8161 on the same
+file). Decompress is unaffected. Round-trip is preserved on every
+real `.kv` file we have and on lz4's own 1080-case verify suite.
+
+Marking the modifications: each edited site carries a single
+`/* ds4: ... */` comment so an upstream re-vendor diff is obvious.
+
 ## Streaming, not snapshot
 
 Compression goes through a `funopen`/`fopencookie` wrapper around
